Find the Minimum Number in an Array

Return the smallest number.

Examples:

[3, 7, 2, 9, 4] → 2
[-5, -2, -10] → -10
[8] → 8

Constraints:

Don't use Math.min().
Try one loop.



Solution:


const num = [3, 7, 2, 9, 4];
let min = num[0];

for (let i = 0; i < num.length; i++) {
  if (min > num[i]) {
    min = num[i];
  }
}

console.log(min);
